"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1839.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":16234,"officials":[{"fullName":"Wes McCauley","displayName":"Wes McCauley","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"James Tobias","displayName":"James Tobias","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Brandon Schrader","displayName":"Brandon Schrader","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Julien Fournier","displayName":"Julien Fournier","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Jacob Fowler makes 46 saves for 2nd shutout of season as Canadiens beat Blues 2-0","description":"— Jacob Fowler made a career-high 46 saves for his second shutout of the season, and Zachary Bolduc and Florian Xhekaj scored as the Montreal Canadiens defeated the St. Louis Blues 2-0 on Tuesday night.","story":"ST. LOUIS -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5188437/jacob-fowler\">Jacob Fowler</a> made a career-high 46 saves for his second shutout of the season, and Zachary Bolduc and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5188457/florian-xhekaj\">Florian Xhekaj</a> scored as the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/mtl/montreal-canadiens\">Montreal Canadiens</a> defeated the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/stl/st-louis-blues\">St. Louis Blues</a> 2-0 on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2976851/mike-matheson\">Mike Matheson</a> had two assists as the Canadiens (7-3-2) improved to 4-1-1 on the road this season with their third straight away victory. Fowler’s shutout was his third in 24 career starts.\n\n\r\n              The Blues (5-6-1) fell to 3-2-1 at home as they were shut out for the second straight game. They lost 4-0 to visiting Carolina on Saturday.\n\n\r\n              Bolduc put the Canadiens ahead with 11:23 left in the second period, slapping a one-timer from the right circle for his fifth goal of the season. Bolduc’s first goal against his former team was assisted by Matheson and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4233880/alexandre-texier\">Alexandre Texier</a>.\n\n\r\n              A first-round draft pick in 2021 by St. Louis, Bolduc scored 19 goals for the Blues during the 2024-25 season before being traded to the Canadiens for defenseman <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4874748/logan-mailloux\">Logan Mailloux</a>. The 23-year-old right winger had 12 goals and 30 points for Montreal in 78 games last season.\n\n\r\n              Xhekaj scored the first goal of his NHL career with 17:43 remaining in the third period off a redirection of a shot by Matheson. Xhekaj’s goal, in his ninth game, was assisted by Matheson and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4565224/kirby-dach\">Kirby Dach</a>.\n\n\r\n              Fowler stopped 24 shots in the third period.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Canadiens: At Dallas on Thursday night.\n\n\r\n              Blues: Host Boston on Thursday night.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-28T02:59:46Z"}}